              "variable": "Onroad.asb_scheduleFractionTotal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "avgspeedbin_rows": 16
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_four_blocks_select_the_same_cohorts_and_emit_different_ones",
          "description": "THE ASSERTION THIS FIXTURE EXISTS FOR. All four pollutant-processes SELECT the same 125 candidates -- `pollutantprocessmappedmodelyear` covers model years 1950-2060 for every one of them. (The per-block selection and rate counts that asserted this are gone from the model, and `cohortSurvivorCount`, which now counts the cohorts the output carries, is 124 rather than the 125 once asserted here; none of these is asserted.) What they EMIT differs: 124 for total NOx, because `emissionratebyage` has no fuel-type-9 / ageGroup-2099 row and the model year 2000 electricity cohort therefore finds no rate; and 104 for each species, because `nono2ratio` has no fuel type 9 row at all. 124 + 3 x 104 = 436, which is `n_outputRate`, recomputed here from the mask (`rateSurvivorCount`) rather than trusted. 312 of the 436 arrive through the chain. The mask and the output ordinal are pinned at two NOx rate rows, one that survives (124, emitted at ordinal 105) and one that does not (164, ordinal 0).\\n\\n`process-brakewear` had these two numbers EQUAL for every block, which is what let it divide an output row number by a block length; `process-refueling` did not, and ranks over the whole rate relation exactly as this does. Asserting BOTH counts is what made the raggedness attributable: it is the rate and the ratio, not the cohort rule -- and 124 + 104 x 3 and 109 x 4 are the same 436, so the total alone does not say which, and with the per-block counts gone this test no longer does either.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rateSurvivorCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 436.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.run_chainedRowCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 312.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_survives",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 124
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_survives",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 164
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_outputOrdinal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 105.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 124
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_outputOrdinal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 164
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_activity_chain_reproduces_the_reference_source_hours",
          "description": "docs/process-nox-speciation.md 6.1, at the four stages a wrong factor shows up at. The activity half is shared by all four pollutant-processes -- the species are scaled from the parent and inherit its activity exactly -- so an error here moves all 872 rows. The `act_sho` values are the snapshot's own `sho` table, which nothing in this document reads.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 2e-06
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.act_travelFraction",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0180442029323595,
              "coords": {
                "activity_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.act_travelFraction",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0016091748533087,
              "coords": {
                "activity_rows": 41
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.act_averageSpeed",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 56.361205525,
              "coords": {
                "activity_rows": 1,
                "roadtype_rows": 4
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.act_sho",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 260.057,
              "coords": {
                "activity_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.act_sho",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 23.1918,
              "coords": {
                "activity_rows": 41
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_collapsed_base_rate_reproduces_the_reference_generator_table",
          "description": "`rtDay_meanBaseRate` IS `baseratebyage_1_2020.meanBaseRate` and `rtDay_meanBaseRateACAdj` IS its `meanBaseRateACAdj` -- the reference's own S14 intermediate, computed here from `emissionratebyage` and W and read from nothing. The table has 248 rows, 124 cohorts x 2 day types, which is the same 124 `pp_rateCohortCount` counts by a completely different route.\\n\\nThe A/C companion column is asserted beside the rate because it is exactly `rate x (fullACAdjustment - 1)` and the two would drift apart if the operating-mode weighting were applied to one and not the other. It is worth asserting even though `rt_acFactor` is 0 and it reaches no emitted number: this is the only place in the document where the A/C rows are checked at all.\\n\\nThe three species carry no rate: `emissionratebyage` has no 3201 row, so J22's inner join leaves rate_row 165 at the additive identity.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 2e-05
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.771623,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 111.39,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 41,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 5.45318,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 82,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.000257317,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 83,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 124,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 165,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRateACAdj",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.295537,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRateACAdj",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 43.7676,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 41,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRateACAdj",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 2.14267,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 82,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRateACAdj",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 9.8554e-05,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 83,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_model_year_group_is_a_property_of_the_pollutant_process",
          "description": "The cohort key that differs between the parent and its species, and the reason the rate relation exists at all. `pollutantprocessmappedmodelyear` maps model year 2020 to modelYearGroup 2020 for 301 -- shortModYrGroupID 40, a two-digit year -- and to modelYearGroup 20112020 for 3201, whose short group is 6, one of six decade bands. Model year 1980 maps to short group 1 for 301. A document that computed one group per cohort would key the ratio lookup on the parent's group and find nothing.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_shortModYrGroupID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 40.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_shortModYrGroupID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 41
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_shortModYrGroupID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 6.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 165
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_modelYearGroupID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 2020.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_modelYearGroupID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 20112020.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 165
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_temperature_factor_is_the_humidity_correction_and_the_AC_arm_is_dead",
          "description": "S15's temperature adjustment, at 59.5 degF. NO cohort in this run finds a `temperatureadjustment` row -- the table's four rows are polProcessID 301, fuel type 2, model years 2027-2060 -- so both terms are 0 by the aggregate's additive identity and the NOx branch reduces to its humidity factor alone. That factor is hand-checkable from `noxhumidityadjust` and `zonemonthhour`: gasoline and E85 take CFR 86, `1 - 0.0329 x (10.053684293477 - 10.71)` = 1.0215927867; diesel takes CFR 1065, `1 / (9.953 x 0.015929059029 + 0.832)` = 1.0095483848; electricity has no row and takes 1. Those two hand-checks are done on the humidity `ZoneMonthHour` STORES, and are kept that way on purpose -- they are the arithmetic a reader can redo -- but since docs/meteorology-generator.md 8.2 this document COMPUTES the humidity instead of reading it, and lands 1.02159279434712 and 1.009548388483679: 7.4418e-09 and 3.6203e-09 from the hand-checked numbers. The five assertions on those two values therefore carry `rel: 1e-7`, and what they now test is the whole chain from `temperature`, `relHumidity` and `County.barometricPressure` down to the factor, against MOVES's own stored answer. The three species are pollutants 32, 33 and 34, so they miss the NOx branch and take the fall-through quadratic, whose coefficients are also 0 -- exactly 1.\\n\\nTHE A/C ARM IS DEAD AND IS ASSERTED DEAD. The A/C activity quadratic is -0.29698 at this heat index -- computed, since 8.2, and 7.934 degF below the 67.4340633418 at which it would cross 0 -- and clamps to 0, so `rt_acFactor` is exactly 0 and the 23 live `fullacadjustment` rows reach no emitted number. Nothing here tests the ORDER in which the criteria ratio and the temperature factor reach the A/C increment.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 1e-09
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_hasTempAdjustExact",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_tempAdjustTermA",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_tempAdjustTermB",
              "time": 0.0,
