          "description": "`NOCalculator` and `NO2Calculator`, entirely, and then the whole chain against the numbers MOVESOutput stores. `nono2ratio` gives 0.836 / 0.156 / 0.008 for gasoline model year 2020 (NO / NO2 / HONO, summing to exactly 1) and 0.80352 for diesel 2020; the ratio is 0 on the parent's own rate path, because the table carries 3201, 3301 and 3401 and nothing else, and 0 on every electricity row, which is what removes that whole column from the species blocks. Rate row 288 is the case that separates the two halves of `rt_survives`: its parent DOES survive -- NOx electricity model year 2020 is emitted, at zero (not asserted here; the parent-survives variable is gone) -- and it still is not, because there is no ratio.\\n\\nThe species carry no direct quantity at all: `rtDay_quantDirect` is exactly 0 at rate rows 165 and 329.\\n\\nThe MOVESOutput rows are chosen so that every factor is exercised and the four blocks can be checked against each other: (MY 1980, gasoline) is the largest rate, (MY 2020, gasoline) the largest activity, (MY 2020, electricity) the zero, and the NO/NO2/HONO triple at (MY 2020, gasoline) sums to its parent's 38.0353 by construction.",
